From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:50:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: a733: Set the withstand voltage of the banks
 with a supply

The withstand mode of the A733 pin banks in GPIO_POW_MOD_SEL is left as
the boot chain set it, except for bank PF. The boot chain on the Radxa
Cubie A7S sets every bank to the adaptive mode; a boot chain that does
not touch the register leaves the reset value 0x022aaaa0, the 3.3V mode
for every bank, also for the banks that run at 1.8V.

Without this, the eMMC on bank PC fails when the bank is in its 3.3V
mode at a 1.8V supply, because the withstand mode of a bank has to
match its supply (user manual section 18.14.4.6). Seen on the Radxa
Cubie A7S: with the PC field at 10 and the eMMC at HS400 enhanced
strobe, raw reads returned no data and the card dropped out:

  mmc2: mmc_select_hs400es failed, error -110

Program the mode from the bank supply with the two-bit variant, for the
banks PC, PD, PE, PG, PH, PJ and PK (fields per user manual section
18.14.6.1). The manual gives the adaptive code for banks PC, PE and PK
as 01 in the register table and as 10 in the text of section 18.14.4.6;
a fixed mode depends on neither. Bank PF keeps its mode with its supply
switch. A bank without a supply in the DT is not written.

With bank PC in the 1.8V mode (11), the eMMC read the same data at
HS400 enhanced strobe as in the adaptive mode, in the same time.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: after boot bank PC was in its 1.8V mode and
the eMMC read the same data at HS400 enhanced strobe, the 3.3V banks
with a requested pin were in their 3.3V mode, and the banks without one
kept the value of the boot chain.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
index 3b8d7dda66fc..c54d1744d152 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -24,6 +24,14 @@ static const u8 a733_irq_bank_muxes[SUNXI_PINCTRL_MAX_BANKS] =
 static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a733_pinctrl_data = {
 	.irq_banks = 11,
 	.pf_power_source = true,
+	.io_bias_cfg_variant = BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL_2BIT,
+	/*
+	 * PC, PD, PE, PG, PH, PJ, PK. PF follows its supply switch, see
+	 * sunxi_pconf_set_power_source(); PB has no field of its own
+	 * and the field of PI is reserved.
+	 */
+	.io_bias_banks = BIT(2) | BIT(3) | BIT(4) | BIT(6) | BIT(7) |
+			 BIT(9) | BIT(10),
 };
 
 static int a733_pinctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
